codex
The translated program uses exactly one two-argument function and no calls from inside it, so the runtime can stay compact: it loads that function, binds tuple arguments, and gives small-step rules to each emitted statement/expression constructor. The loop remains an actual loop in the runtime; any proof acceleration will live separately in `verification.k`.
