Concrete `krun` execution now agrees with all three prompt examples, including the non-intersection and length-two prime cases. I’ve also separated the proof into an inductive loop lemma and a whole-program claim, so the trial-division loop is checked against a recursive primality reference before that lemma is used to discharge the endpoint-level theorem.
